# data-models-relationships

## Core Classification Models

### Bond Classifications
- No Bond: Special status indicating detention without bond option
- Numeric Bond: Standard monetary bond amounts with validation rules
- Refer to Magistrate: Cases requiring manual judicial review
- Summons: Non-monetary release agreements
- Unsecured: Bond amounts without immediate payment requirement

### Time Bucket Hierarchy
- 0-24 Hours: Immediate processing window
- 24-48 Hours: Standard processing window
- 48-72 Hours: Extended processing window
- 3-7 Days: Follow-up window
- 7-30 Days: Monitoring window
- 30-60 Days: Long-term tracking
- 60+ Days: Archive window

## Entity Relationships

### Case Management
- BondCase -> Client (1:1)
- BondCase -> Cosigners (1:Many)
- BondCase -> CheckIns (1:Many)
- BondCase -> Documents (1:Many)
- BondCase -> Payments (1:Many)

### Organization Structure
- Department -> County (Many:1)
- Department -> Cases (1:Many)
- Department -> Users (1:Many)
- User -> Role (Many:1)

### Contact Verification
- Client -> EnrichmentData (1:Many)
- EnrichmentData -> Provider (Many:1)
- EnrichmentData -> Addresses (1:Many)
- EnrichmentData -> Relationships (1:Many)

## Data Enrichment Models
- Person Search Results
  - Contact Normalization Rules
  - Address Standardization
  - Relationship Scoring
  - Risk Assessment Factors

## Critical Business Rules
- Bond amounts must be normalized across jurisdictions
- Time buckets determine case priorities and workflows
- Department access is scoped to specific counties
- Enrichment data expires after configurable windows
- Check-in schedules follow jurisdiction-specific rules

